  description: Random Access Memory (RAM) is a temporary storage component that holds
    data and instructions currently being used by the CPU. Unlike permanent storage
    devices such as SSDs, the data stored in RAM is erased when the computer is powered
    off. Installing more RAM can improve a computer's multitasking performance.
